---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Using the enrolment prototype" actor={Astro.locals.actor}>
  <h1>From finding a course to enrolling</h1>
  <ol class="help-list">
    <li>
      <strong>Create and verify your account.</strong> Use an @anu.edu.au address and a separate prototype
      password. Open the emailed link and confirm, then sign in.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Explore courses.</strong> Search by full code, number, or title. Use the subject filter to
      distinguish codes such as COMP6528 and ENGN6528.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Build your semester.</strong> Open a course, choose its offering, and save it. A saved course is
      not an enrolment.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Resolve permission requirements.</strong> Read the comparison with your fictional academic
      record and send a request attached to that offering. Its history shows who has it. If a recorded
      prerequisite is wrong, request human review.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Confirm enrolment.</strong> Ready courses and approved requests can be confirmed individually.
      Pending requests do not stop you enrolling in other courses.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Your academic profile</h2>
  <p>
    Your account gets a fictional Master of Computing (Advanced) record with foundation subjects. It is
    demonstration data, not a connection to ANU's student records. View it under My profile.
  </p>
  <h2>For reviewers</h2>
  <p>
    Staff accounts are invitation-only. A reviewer sees requests for their assigned courses, the student's
    explanation, the relevant eligibility checks, and the request history. Approval and rejection are
    recorded; rejection requires a reason.
  </p>
  <h2>About the dataset</h2>
  <p>
    Find courses and the course library use the same supplied 2027 pages, including descriptions, learning
    outcomes, requirements and offerings. Only a subset of requirements has an automated eligibility check;
    all other courses say that a check is unavailable. Existing requests retain their original year.
    All reviewer identities and academic records are fictional. Degree and specialisation planning is not yet implemented.
  </p>
  <h2>Account help</h2>
  <p>
    Verification links last 30 minutes. Request a new one from the sign-in page. Password recovery is not yet
    available; use a separate password you can retain for this prototype.
  </p>
</Layout>
